"""
Non-lifting bluff-body drag acting at a single point.

Intended for the fuselage, canopy, undercarriage and any other item that
adds drag without a lift curve. The drag area is given separately per body
axis,

    F = -0.5 * rho * |v| * [CdA_x*v_x, CdA_y*v_y, CdA_z*v_z]

with `v` the velocity of the mounting point through the air mass, resolved
in `frame_a`. A slender fuselage has a small axial drag area and a much
larger lateral and normal one, and the anisotropy is what makes the body
produce a side force in sideslip at all.

# Where to mount it

Mount `frame_a` at the body's **centre of pressure**, not at its centroid:
for a slender body that is roughly a quarter of the body length behind the
nose, well ahead of the aircraft centre of gravity. The normal and side
forces then act ahead of the CG and generate the destabilising pitching and
yawing moment of the fuselage (the Munk moment) directly out of the
multibody geometry, which is what the fin and tailplane have to be sized
against. Mounting it at the CG silently removes that moment and makes the
aircraft look more stable than it is.

Several instances may be strung along a fuselage if a single point is too
coarse.

# Numerical conditioning

`|v|` is formed as `sqrt(v.v + v_eps^2)`, so the force is smooth through
zero velocity and vanishes there; the component is safe at rest.

No torque is applied: a point drag force has no couple of its own.
"""
component DragBody
  "Mount at the body's centre of pressure"
  frame_a = Frame3D() {^frame_a}
  "Density and wind at the body"
  air = AirState() {^air}
  "Drag area Cd*S for motion along the body x axis"
  parameter CdA_x::Area = 0.05
  "Drag area Cd*S for motion along the body y axis"
  parameter CdA_y::Area = 1.0
  "Drag area Cd*S for motion along the body z axis"
  parameter CdA_z::Area = 1.0
  "Speed below which the drag is faded out; keep well below any flight speed"
  parameter v_eps::Velocity = 0.5
  "Velocity of the mounting point relative to the air mass, world frame"
  variable v_rel_0::Velocity[3]
  "Velocity of the mounting point relative to the air mass, body frame"
  variable v_rel_s::Velocity[3]
  "Regularised speed through the air"
  variable V::Velocity
  "Drag force applied to frame_a, body frame"
  variable F_s::Dyad.Force[3]
  "Magnitude of the drag force"
  variable D::Dyad.Force
relations
  v_rel_0 = der(frame_a.r_0) - [air.v_wind_x, air.v_wind_y, air.v_wind_z]
  v_rel_s = MultibodyComponents.resolve2(frame_a.R, v_rel_0)
  V = sqrt(v_rel_s[1] ^ 2 + v_rel_s[2] ^ 2 + v_rel_s[3] ^ 2 + v_eps ^ 2)
  F_s = -0.5 * air.rho * V * [CdA_x * v_rel_s[1], CdA_y * v_rel_s[2], CdA_z * v_rel_s[3]]
  D = sqrt(F_s[1] ^ 2 + F_s[2] ^ 2 + F_s[3] ^ 2)
  frame_a.f = -F_s
  frame_a.tau = [0, 0, 0]
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://Multtest/DragBody.svg"}},
  "_links": {
    "frame_a": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": -50, "y1": 450, "x2": 50, "y2": 550}}}
    },
    "air": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 450, "y1": -50, "x2": 550, "y2": 50}}}
    }
  }
}
end

"""
Terminal velocity of a body dropped from rest with isotropic drag.

The steady state must satisfy `m*g = 0.5*rho*CdA*v^2`, so the body settles
at `v = sqrt(2*m*g/(rho*CdA))`. This is the dynamic check on the component:
the drag is the only thing balancing gravity, so getting the magnitude or
the sign wrong is immediately visible.
"""
test component TestDragTerminal
  world = MultibodyComponents.World() {^world}
  body = MultibodyComponents.Body(m = 1.0, orientation_state = MultibodyComponents.OrientationState.Quaternion(), statePriority = 1000, linearStatePriority = 1000) {^body}
  drag = DragBody(CdA_x = 0.5, CdA_y = 0.5, CdA_z = 0.5) {^drag}
relations
  drag.air.rho = 1.225
  drag.air.v_wind_x = 0
  drag.air.v_wind_y = 0
  drag.air.v_wind_z = 0
  connect(body.frame_a, drag.frame_a) {^id1}
metadata {
  "_links": {
    "world": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 60, "y1": 620, "x2": 160, "y2": 720}}}},
    "body": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 300, "y1": 330, "x2": 400, "y2": 430}}}},
    "drag": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 640, "y1": 330, "x2": 740, "y2": 430}}}},
    "id1": {"Dyad": {"edges": [{"S": 1, "M": [], "E": 2}]}}
  }
}
end

"""
Direction sweep at constant speed, to check the per-axis drag areas.

The mounting point is driven at a constant speed whose direction turns
through a full circle in the body x-y plane; each force component must
follow `-0.5*rho*|v|*CdA_i*v_i` with its own drag area.
"""
test component TestDragAnisotropy
  world = MultibodyComponents.World(render = false) {^world}
  mover = MultibodyComponents.PrescribedVelocity(r_start = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], render = false) {^mover}
  drag = DragBody(CdA_x = 0.08, CdA_y = 1.2, CdA_z = 0.9) {^drag}
  "Speed held constant through the sweep"
  parameter V_test::Velocity = 30.0
  "Duration of one full turn of the velocity vector"
  parameter t_sweep::Time = 1.0
  "Direction of the velocity vector in the body x-y plane"
  variable phi::Angle
relations
  phi = 2 * 3.141592653589793 * time / t_sweep
  mover.v_x = V_test * cos(phi)
  mover.v_y = V_test * sin(phi)
  mover.v_z = 0
  drag.air.rho = 1.225
  drag.air.v_wind_x = 0
  drag.air.v_wind_y = 0
  drag.air.v_wind_z = 0
  connect(mover.frame_b, drag.frame_a) {^id1}
metadata {
  "_links": {
    "world": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 60, "y1": 620, "x2": 160, "y2": 720}}}},
    "mover": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 300, "y1": 330, "x2": 400, "y2": 430}}}},
    "drag": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 640, "y1": 330, "x2": 740, "y2": 430}}}},
    "id1": {"Dyad": {"edges": [{"S": 1, "M": [], "E": 2}]}}
  }
}
end